<title>POLAND: POLAND C/A DEFICIT UP TO $2.274 BLN IN JAN-APRIL.</title>
<headline>POLAND C/A DEFICIT UP TO $2.274 BLN IN JAN-APRIL.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland had a current account</p>
<p>deficit of $742 million in April, after a $408 million gap in</p>
<p>March, bringing the shortfall in the January-April period to</p>
<p>$2.274 billion, the National Bank of Poland said on Wednesday.</p>
<p> POLISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	   APRIL	  MARCH     APRIL 96</p>
<p> current account mln USD	  -742	 -408 (-355)   -377</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	-935	 -885	    -520</p>
<p> exports			     2,361	1,920	   1,968</p>
<p> imports			     3,296	2,805	   2,488</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	536	  423	     629</p>
<p>				     JAN-APRIL 1997    JAN-ARPIL 1996</p>
<p> current account mln USD	  -2,274		-226</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	-4,002	    -1,962</p>
<p> exports				 8,127	     7,505</p>
<p> imports				12,129	     9,467</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	1,752	     2,449</p>
<p>Note. Revised figures in brackets. From January 1996 the</p>
<p>central bank introduced a new category, &quot;unclassified flows&quot;</p>
<p>which encompasses mainly unregistered cross-border trade flows.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
